  "caption": "Figure 1. Constructed DEMO of routing-limited rainwater storage. (a) Exactly three roof branches feed two tanks; only the single central branch is split. Arrows show water routing, not pipe dimensions. Tank labels give initial volume / capacity. Loads withdraw continuously and spills leave by separate drains. (b) All three schedules independently start from the same initial state. Bars sum all four one-minute spill records for both tanks; W or E identifies the spilling tank. The right column retains each tank's unused capacity. Net addition exceeds initial free space by 2 L; fixed tenth attains this bound. No field data or forecast uncertainty is represented.",
  "alt_text": "A single central roof stream splits between two disconnected tanks. Fixed third spills 28 L from W with 26 L free in E; delayed tenth spills 7 L from W with 5 L free in E; fixed tenth spills 2 L from E and fills both tanks. All quantities are constructed DEMO values.",
  "source_reference_base": "example_root"
}